Z||000002||Eric||06-15-2000||11:16 AM||||I know about the riceboy page.  It's pretty funny, but the sticker he is selling isn't.  It just says "riceboypage.com".  Most people, who didn't already know about it, would get confused and maybe crash their SUV in the the back of your Fiero.  A new more creative sticker would help to educate more youngsters.  Afterall, a lot of these 16 year olds have never even heard of Fieros.  For all we know, they may see our cars and think "That looks cool" and try to emulate us by putting a Fiero wing on the back of their parent's Accord and FORMULA stickers all over it.  So my point is, we have to establish boundries between ourselves and these riceboy posers.  I think a sticker would be a good way of doing this.||||reg||1
